== 2.10 Chapter 2 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The part of the brain that controls balance and coordination is the],
  [cerebellum],
  [hypothalamus],
  [cerebrum],
  [medulla oblongata]
)

#mcq(2, [Breathing rate and heart rate are controlled by the],
  [medulla oblongata],
  [cerebrum],
  [pituitary],
  [cerebellum]
)

#mcq(3, [The part of the brain that is the seat of intelligence and memory is the],
  [cerebrum],
  [hypothalamus],
  [cerebellum],
  [medulla]
)

#mcq(4, [In the spinal cord, grey matter is found],
  [in a butterfly-shaped core surrounded by white matter],
  [nowhere],
  [only on the outside],
  [only at the very ends]
)

#mcq(5, [Myopia is corrected with a],
  [prism],
  [cylindrical lens],
  [convex lens],
  [concave lens]
)

#mcq(6, [The part of the eye that controls the amount of light entering is the],
  [iris],
  [cornea],
  [lens],
  [retina]
)

#mcq(7, [Accommodation is the ability of the eye to],
  [control the amount of light entering],
  [focus objects at different distances by changing the shape of the lens],
  [see in colour],
  [produce tears]
)

#mcq(8, [The receptors for hearing are found in the],
  [Eustachian tube],
  [semicircular canals],
  [eardrum],
  [cochlea]
)

#mcq(9, [The ossicles of the middle ear function to],
  [detect the direction of sound],
  [equalise pressure],
  [keep the ear clean],
  [amplify the vibration and pass it to the oval window]
)

#mcq(10, [When a person moves from a bright room into a dark one, the pupils],
  [dilate to let in more light],
  [constrict to let in less light],
  [stay the same size],
  [close completely]
)

#mcq(11, [The image formed on the retina is],
  [not formed at all],
  [the same size and upright],
  [inverted and smaller than the object],
  [upright and larger]
)

#mcq(12, [A person who can see distant objects clearly but cannot read a book at arm's length has],
  [myopia],
  [astigmatism],
  [a cataract],
  [hypermetropia]
)

#mcq(13, [The blind spot is the point on the retina where],
  [the iris meets the sclera],
  [the cornea joins the sclera],
  [the optic nerve leaves the eye and there are no receptors],
  [the lens is attached]
)

#mcq(14, [Rods differ from cones in that rods],
  [work only in bright light],
  [detect colour only],
  [are found in the iris],
  [work in dim light but do not distinguish colour]
)

#mcq(15, [The cornea is important because it],
  [contains the receptors],
  [refracts light as it enters the eye],
  [produces tears],
  [controls the pupil size]
)

#mcq(16, [The Eustachian tube connects the middle ear to the],
  [outer ear],
  [throat],
  [eye],
  [brain]
)

#mcq(17, [Which receptors detect pain?],
  [Cones],
  [Rods],
  [Free nerve endings],
  [Touch corpuscles]
)

#mcq(18, [The three ossicles are the],
  [rods, cones and iris],
  [malleus, incus and stapes],
  [pinna, canal and eardrum],
  [cochlea, utricle and saccus]
)

#mcq(19, [Damage to the cerebellum would most likely cause],
  [loss of memory],
  [inability to breathe],
  [blindness],
  [loss of balance and jerky movement]
)

#mcq(20, [Which of these is a voluntary action?],
  [Blinking],
  [Sneezing],
  [Writing your name],
  [Pupil constriction]
)

#mcq(21, [The retina contains],
  [rods and cones],
  [the ciliary muscles],
  [the lens and iris],
  [the optic nerve only]
)

#mcq(22, [A concave lens is used to correct myopia because it],
  [makes the pupil smaller],
  [converges the light more strongly],
  [diverges the light before it enters the eye],
  [changes the colour of light]
)

#mcq(23, [The grey matter of the brain is found],
  [in the spinal nerves],
  [in the pituitary],
  [only in the centre],
  [on the outer surface as the cortex]
)

#mcq(24, [Which structure protects the eye and keeps its shape?],
  [Retina],
  [Sclera],
  [Lens],
  [Iris]
)

#mcq(25, [The function of the semicircular canals is to],
  [detect sound],
  [amplify sound],
  [detect the position and movement of the head],
  [equalise pressure]
)

#mcq(26, [A reflex action that involves the spinal cord is faster than a voluntary action because],
  [there are no synapses involved],
  [the muscle is stronger],
  [the impulse travels faster in the cord],
  [the impulse does not have to travel to the brain and back]
)

#mcq(27, [The optic nerve carries impulses],
  [from the brain to the retina],
  [from the retina to the cerebrum],
  [from the lens to the iris],
  [from the ear to the brain]
)

#mcq(28, [Presbyopia is the],
  [clouding of the lens],
  [inability to see colour],
  [loss of lens elasticity with age, making near vision difficult],
  [detachment of the retina]
)

#mcq(29, [Which part of the brain links the nervous and endocrine systems?],
  [Hypothalamus],
  [Cerebellum],
  [Medulla],
  [Corpus callosum]
)

#mcq(30, [The pupil appears black because],
  [it contains no receptors],
  [no light is reflected back out of the eye],
  [it is filled with black pigment],
  [it is covered by the iris]
)

